  "slug": "phylogenomic-models-e281",
  "summary": "Open benchmarks of gene prediction, binding free energy, and backbone generation methods now test tools against blinded or unified evaluation frameworks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evaluation rigor for computational prediction and design tools. Several items pair new or updated methods with explicit benchmarking: geneML reports higher gene-level F1 than BRAKER3 on fungal genomes, OpenFE is assessed through a blinded and public benchmark spanning 15 pharmaceutical companies and over 1,700 ligands, and Scaffold-Lab ranks seven protein backbone generation methods on designability, novelty, diversity, and efficiency. A review of antimicrobial peptide prediction tools identifies data leakage and inconsistent evaluation and proposes a reference framework, while PyRMD Studio uses Butina-cluster splits to limit leakage. The shared emphasis is standardized, leakage-aware comparison rather than individual tool performance alone. InterProScan 6 and OMEGA extend the set with workflow reimplementation and open-source gene assembly, respectively.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
